Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:25:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 29/40] Metal diamond engine: Mur faces of one axis share a
 barrier; blocks of nearly equal depth (snapshot cg30a)

Mur faces of one axis have no cell in common and none writes another one's shift line, so consecutive faces of one
axis in the Apply order share a barrier, and in a tile whose faces are all on one axis each thread does Post and
Apply of its elements in one go (OPENEMS_DIAMOND_MURMERGE=0: as before). The rest of a call that is not a multiple
of K steps is spread over blocks of nearly equal depth: 10 steps at K=4 are 4, 3, 3 and not 4, 4, 2
(OPENEMS_DIAMOND_EVEN=0). The fields do not depend on either: diamond_check.sh 72 of 72 identical.

Generated-by: Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
